photo.light,0.0,,T2,,,recomputed every step from the state; the config value is overwritten,unit_check,"runtime slot, not an input. Its presence in the config file is misleading and it should be removed from the parameter table"
photo.limitation_of_photosynthetic_rate,0.5,,T2,,,"Runtime slot. Recomputed every step by limitation_of_photosynthetic_rate(starch, lambda_c, max_starch) (src/model/carbohydrates.c) and written back into Input by plant_outputs_apply_to_input() (src/model/outputs.c); Tedone Eq 2.2.2 C = lambda_c + (1-lambda_c)(amax-a)/amax. The config value 0.5 is never read.",recomputed,"INERT: measured, not assumed -- tools/inertness_probe.c perturbed this key over a wide two-point range from the clean-HEAD baseline in all three photosynthesis modes; max change in final biomass/starch/sucrose/nitrogen was 0.0000%. Not a parameter of the model as built."
photo.max_photosynthetic_rate,12.7,umolC6/(gFW h),T3,Tedone2020,"Eq 2.2.1, §2.2.2",,read_paper,code value 12.7 equals paper value 12.7
photo.nitrogen_saturation,0.45,,T2,,,"Runtime slot. Recomputed every step as 2n/(n+n_min)-1 (src/model/nutrients.c:48), zero below threshold, then written back by plant_outputs_apply_to_input(). The config value 0.45 is never read.",recomputed,"INERT: measured, not assumed -- tools/inertness_probe.c perturbed this key over a wide two-point range from the clean-HEAD baseline in all three photosynthesis modes; max change in final biomass/starch/sucrose/nitrogen was 0.0000%. Not a parameter of the model as built."
photo.phosphorus_saturation,0.45,,T2,,,"Runtime slot. Recomputed every step from the optimal stoichiometric ratio (src/model/nutrients.c:58), then written back by plant_outputs_apply_to_input(). The config value 0.45 is never read.",recomputed,"INERT: measured, not assumed -- tools/inertness_probe.c perturbed this key over a wide two-point range from the clean-HEAD baseline in all three photosynthesis modes; max change in final biomass/starch/sucrose/nitrogen was 0.0000%. Not a parameter of the model as built."
growth.leaf_biomass,0.02,gFW,T2,,input.c:14; default.config:15,"initial condition of a state variable, not a free parameter",unit_check,"present in code, not stated in the source model -- needs a source or a T5 declaration; has its own ODE; the config entry sets t=0 only"
growth.root_biomass,0.02,gFW,T2,,input.c:15; default.config:16,"initial condition of a state variable, not a free parameter",unit_check,"present in code, not stated in the source model -- needs a source or a T5 declaration; has its own ODE; the config entry sets t=0 only"
growth.total_biomass,0.04,gFW,T2,,input.c:16; default.config:17,"initial condition of a state variable, not a free parameter",unit_check,"present in code, not stated in the source model -- needs a source or a T5 declaration; has its own ODE; the config entry sets t=0 only"
photo.min_leaf_biomass,0.001,gFW,T4,,,"Structural guard, not a measured quantity: photosynthesis() returns 0 when leaf_biomass < min_leaf_biomass (src/model/photosynthesis.c:108,136,182). Bounded above by the initial leaf biomass B_l(0)=0.02 gFW, which the guard must not exceed or the plant cannot start; 0.001 is 20x below it.",recomputed,"INERT at the shipped value: perturbing 1e-4..1e-2 changed nothing in any mode (the trajectory never approaches 0.02 gFW from above). Tedone assumes B_l^min = B_l without giving a number (docs/revision/handoff/tedone_parameters.json). Reported as a guard, never as a fitted or measured parameter."
photo.feedback_on_photosynthesis,0.62,-,T5,,,,recomputed,"INERT IN THE PRODUCTION MODE. model_report.c:119 selects PHOTO_MODE_FARQUHAR_JARVIS, and farquhar_photosynthesis() never reads limitation_of_photosynthetic_rate. Measured (trackE): sweeping lambda_c over 0.10-0.99 leaves ph = 10.9509019852 constant to 10 dp. The per-photoperiod fitted values 0.82/0.79/0.67/0.62 have NO effect in the mode the paper runs; they are live only in PHOTO_MODE_BASIC. Tedone Eq 2.2.2 is bypassed. Also means the starch feedback -- and hence the max_starch ceiling -- is unenforced."
carbohydrates.max_starch,10.0,umolC6/gFW,T6,,,Recomputed every step as max_starch_degradation_rate*(24-photoperiod) = 6*(24-P) = 120/108/96/72 at 4/6/8/12 h.,recomputed,"T6 UNSOURCED and structurally defective. (a) Reuses tau_as_max = 6 umolC6 gFW-1 h-1 (Appendix A), a degradation RATE, as a CAPACITY; no thesis statement supports the identification. (b) SPLIT VALUE: the overwrite at algebraic.c:41 sits BETWEEN its two consumers, so min_nitrogen()/min_phosphorus() (:31,:37) receive the stale config 10.0 while limitation_of_photosynthetic_rate() (:49) receives 6*(24-P) -- one symbol, two quantities, differing 7.2-12x per step. Fixing the order costs MAPE 3.33 -> 11.76, integrability 4/4 held. (c) The feedback that consumes it is INERT in PHOTO_MODE_FARQUHAR_JARVIS (the production mode), so the ceiling is unenforced: starch reaches 32909 at kappa 1.60 against a ceiling of 72, and clamping lim at 0 is bit-identical. Integrability stays 4/4 throughout -- the model goes unphysical silently, it does not diverge. Dusk starch at HEAD reaches 0.904 of the ceiling at 12 h."
carbohydrates.max_starch_degradation_rate,6.0,umolC6/(gFW h),T3,Tedone2020,§2.2.4,,read_paper,code value 6.0 equals paper value 6
photo.photoperiod,8.0,h,T1,Sulpice2014,"Methods / Supplemental Table 1 (4, 6, 8, 12 h treatments)",,read_paper,"EXPERIMENTAL CONDITION, not a fitted parameter: the photoperiod treatments are the independent variable of the reference experiment and are stated in the source. Retained at T1 on that basis. DEFECT unchanged: src/model/input.c:21 defaults to 12.0 h while config/default.config sets 8.0 h, so a run that does not load the config silently uses a different photoperiod."
nutrients.optimal_stoichiometric_ratio,10.0,umolN/umolP,T3,Tedone2020,"Eq 2.2.7, Eq 2.2.31",,read_paper,code value 10.0 equals paper value 10
carbohydrates.starch_partition_coeff,0.6,-,T2,,input.c:25; default.config:24,"initial condition of a state variable, not a free parameter",unit_check,"present in code, not stated in the source model -- needs a source or a T5 declaration; has its own ODE; the config entry sets t=0 only"
carbohydrates.starch_degradation_rate,0.0,,T2,,,recomputed every step from the state; the config value is overwritten,unit_check,"runtime slot, not an input. Its presence in the config file is misleading and it should be removed from the parameter table"
carbohydrates.uptake_cost,0.0,umol C6 gFW-1 h-1,T2,Tedone2020,§2.2.8 (n_c*U_N + p_c*U_P); config entry is a slot,"0.68*nitrogen_uptake + 0.308*phosphorus_uptake, verified against the trajectory to 6.5e-7",recomputed,"DEFECT FOUND AND MEASURED 2026-08-15. In committed HEAD src/model/algebraic.c the uptake_cost() call at :86 reads s.nutrients.nitrogen_uptake and phosphorus_uptake, which are assigned ~41 lines later at :127/:131; both hold their initial 0.0, so uptake_cost is EXACTLY 0 (verified min=max=0 over 27,635 trajectory rows at all four photoperiods). After moving the call below the two assignments the diel-mean becomes 0.359/0.469/0.532/0.593 at 4/6/8/12 h = 14-19% of gross assimilation. CAUTION: the sinks block of tools/model_report.c recomputes uptake_cost from the INITIAL Input (whose uptake fields are 0.0), so its share_uptake metric reads 0.000 whether or not the fix is applied -- it cannot be used as evidence about this term."
carbohydrates.transport_cost,0.0,,T2,,,computed in the model at run time from other quantities,unit_check,"config entry is a slot, not an independent parameter"
carbohydrates.respiration_frequency,0.79,1/h,T3,Tedone2020,"Section 2.2.8 (Costs), ""r_m_bar = 0.79 1/h""",paper states r_m_bar = 0.79 1/h,read_paper,"LOCATOR CORRECTED: the ledger cited Eq 2.2.30, which is r_t_m = r_t_bar(r_m*s + eta*r_g) -- the transport-cost equation. It contains r_m as a symbol but does not state its value. The value 0.79 1/h is stated in prose in Section 2.2.8 (Costs), verified verbatim in docs/revision/tedone_paper_text.txt. The tier stands at T3 (the value is genuinely in the source); only the locator was wrong. Replaces the earlier circular basis ""Calibrated; +-50% around default 0.79"". Independent support, recomputed this session from data/paper/N_data.csv (n=14 leaf respiration means at 23/18 C): 46.28 nmol CO2 gDW-1 s-1 = 166.6 umol CO2 gDW-1 h-1 = 27.77 umolC6 gDW-1 h-1, /12 at FW/DW = 12 gives 2.31 umolC6 gFW-1 h-1. This is a consistency check on the magnitude, NOT the provenance of 0.79 -- the source of the value is Tedone."
carbohydrates.sucrose_loading_frequency,1.98,1/h,T3,Tedone2020,§2.2.8 (Eq 2.2.28),"inherited value RETAINED, but now known to be inconsistent with the measured carbon budget. T4 bound derived this session from Sulpice2014 mmc3: eta must satisfy G_biomass/I <= eta <= (A-R)/I, where I is the diel integral of the loading substrate over the MEASURED sucrose trace. Admissible intervals per photoperiod (min-form): 4h [0.49,0.61], 6h [1.21,1.34], 8h [1.85,1.94], 12h [2.98,3.04] 1/h. 1.98 lies OUTSIDE all four; so does the fitted 6.784468. The bound is photoperiod-dependent because the measured export requirement rises 5.83x from 4h to 12h while the measured 24h mean sucrose rises only 1.07x, so no constant eta can satisfy it under any f(s). See docs/revision/loading_law.md B.",measured_this_session,"DO NOT re-fit. A fitted 6.78 is outside the physically derived bound at every photoperiod and is evidence against the first-order form, not a parameter estimate. Value kept at the paper's 1.98 pending an equation change."
carbohydrates.night_efficiency_starch,0.5,-,T2,,input.c:31; default.config:30,recomputed every step from the state; the config value is overwritten,unit_check,"runtime slot, not an input. Its presence in the config file is misleading and it should be removed from the parameter table"
carbohydrates.max_sucrose,2.0,umolC6/gFW,T3,Tedone2020,§2.2.4 (Eq 2.2.28),"inherited. Measured this session on the model trajectory: the min() clamp is active for only 0.000/0.017/0.153/0.387 of the diel cycle at 4/6/8/12h, so at the shipped eta it is nearly inert and its FORM is weakly identified by any of the model's own measures. In the MEASURED series (data/paper/sugars_starch_reference.csv) sucrose exceeds 2.0 in 77-100% of samples, i.e. the ceiling is set below the observed operating range. Replacing min(s,s_max) by s_max*s/(s+s_max) or by no bound changes every diel measure by <=2.2% once runs are compared at matched realized export flux.",measured_this_session,"s_max=2.0 is below the measured sucrose range at every photoperiod, which is a T1-vs-T3 conflict in the value, independent of the functional form. Form is NOT identifiable from the present measures; see docs/revision/loading_law.md A."
carbohydrates.min_sucrose,1.3,umolC6/gFW,T3,Tedone2020,§2.2.4,,read_paper,code value 1.3 equals paper value 1.3
carbohydrates.starch_night_start,2.0,umolC6/gFW,T2,,,"Runtime slot. The production path sets .starch_night_start = input->carbohydrates.starch at the light-to-dark transition (src/simulation/simulation.c:480). A second static-variable implementation at src/simulation/simulation.c:394-411 carries the comment ""TODO: Remove or wire this function into production flow; it is currently unused by the main simulation path"". The config value 2.0 is never read.",recomputed,"INERT: measured, not assumed -- tools/inertness_probe.c perturbed this key over a wide two-point range from the clean-HEAD baseline in all three photosynthesis modes; max change in final biomass/starch/sucrose/nitrogen was 0.0000%. Not a parameter of the model as built."
carbohydrates.min_starch,0.15,umolC6/gFW,T3,Tedone2020,§2.2.4,,read_paper,code value 0.15 equals paper value 0.15
