gas_exchange.respiration_rate,1.5,,T2,,,computed in the model at run time from other quantities,unit_check,"config entry is a slot, not an independent parameter"
gas_exchange.light_limited_photosynthesis,10.0,,T2,,,computed in the model at run time from other quantities,unit_check,"config entry is a slot, not an independent parameter"
gas_exchange.electron_transport_rate,90.0,,T5,,,,crossref_api,"Jmax, TIER LOWERED T1->T5. Bernacchi et al. 2001 is a TOBACCO study: the abstract (fetched via DOI 10.1111/j.1365-3040.2001.00668.x) states the temperature responses were derived in ""transgenic tobacco containing only 10% normal levels of Rubisco"" and validated in lemon. It reports temperature-response FUNCTIONS (normalised activation energies), not an Arabidopsis capacity at 25 C, so the shipped value cannot be located at the stated locator in the stated source. Full text is not open access (oa_status bronze; unpaywall/PMC/S2/TDM all failed), so the locator could not be checked directly either. No substitute primary source with a locatable Arabidopsis value was found via Crossref/OpenAlex. LIVE: 331.9% change when perturbed 50-200. Note Jmax/Vcmax = 90/45 = 2.00 exactly, a round ratio that is itself the signature of a chosen rather than measured pair. 0 observations named."
gas_exchange.rubisco_limited_photosynthesis,12.0,,T2,,,computed in the model at run time from other quantities,unit_check,"config entry is a slot, not an independent parameter"
gas_exchange.max_rubisco_carboxylation_rate,45.0,,T5,,,,crossref_api,"Vcmax, TIER LOWERED T1->T5. Bernacchi et al. 2001 is a TOBACCO study: the abstract (fetched via DOI 10.1111/j.1365-3040.2001.00668.x) states the temperature responses were derived in ""transgenic tobacco containing only 10% normal levels of Rubisco"" and validated in lemon. It reports temperature-response FUNCTIONS (normalised activation energies), not an Arabidopsis capacity at 25 C, so the shipped value cannot be located at the stated locator in the stated source. Full text is not open access (oa_status bronze; unpaywall/PMC/S2/TDM all failed), so the locator could not be checked directly either. No substitute primary source with a locatable Arabidopsis value was found via Crossref/OpenAlex. LIVE and strongly so: 425.8% change in final state when perturbed 20-120, so this is a consequential fitted parameter, not a harmless default. 0 observations named."
gas_exchange.oxygen_concentration,210.0,,T4,,,"Atmospheric O2 mole fraction: 20.95% of dry air = 209.5 mmol mol-1, rounded to 210. This is a physical constant of the growth atmosphere, not a plant property, so it needs no plant source.",unit_check,"Was T1 citing Bernacchi2001:Table 1. TIER LOWERED T1->T5. Bernacchi et al. 2001 is a TOBACCO study: the abstract (fetched via DOI 10.1111/j.1365-3040.2001.00668.x) states the temperature responses were derived in ""transgenic tobacco containing only 10% normal levels of Rubisco"" and validated in lemon. It reports temperature-response FUNCTIONS (normalised activation energies), not an Arabidopsis capacity at 25 C, so the shipped value cannot be located at the stated locator in the stated source. Full text is not open access (oa_status bronze; unpaywall/PMC/S2/TDM all failed), so the locator could not be checked directly either. No substitute primary source with a locatable Arabidopsis value was found via Crossref/OpenAlex. Re-tiered T4 (bounded by the composition of air) rather than T5, because the value is not free: any figure other than ~210 mmol mol-1 would misdescribe ambient air. LIVE (115.8% change over a 105-420 perturbation), so the bound matters."
gas_exchange.leaf_temperature,25.0,,T5,Sulpice2014,"Methods, growth conditions (states 21/19 C, NOT 25 C)",,read_paper,"TIER LOWERED T1->T5. The row cannot be T1: the source states 21/19 C day/night and the model ships 25 C, so the shipped value does NOT appear at the stated locator -- the ledger's own note already recorded the mismatch while leaving the tier at ""measured"". A T1 row must carry the value the source states. 25 C is instead the temperature at which the Farquhar constants are conventionally normalised, i.e. a modelling choice. Part of the light-and-temperature confound in docs/revision/light_dose_study.md."
gas_exchange.relative_humidity,60.0,,T6,,,,read_paper,"TIER LOWERED T1->T6 (unsourced). The ledger's own note conceded that 60% ""is plausible for a growth cabinet but is not stated in the source"", which is the definition of unsourced -- it cannot stand at T1. Neither Sulpice 2014 nor the Atkinson & Atkin description states a humidity. Work-list item: obtain the chamber humidity from the experimenters, or drop the Jarvis VPD term's dependence on an invented number."
gas_exchange.leaf_water_potential,-0.6,,T5,,,,read_paper,"TIER LOWERED T1->T5. The Jarvis water-potential term uses psi = -0.6 MPa against psi_min = -1.5 MPa (paper/v1/cas-sc-template.tex), but neither ""MPa"" nor ""-1.5"" nor any psi symbol occurs anywhere in docs/revision/tedone_paper_text.txt, and no other source is cited. The reference plants were hydroponic and well-watered, so a mild -0.6 MPa is plausible, but plausible is not sourced. 0 observations named."
"model.nutrient_ratio_pool (structural, not a config key)","max(pool,0)",-,T4,,,"Saturating ratios N/(N+N_min), max_N/(N+max_N), (N-R*P)/(N+R*P) and R/(R+N/P) are bounded and monotone on the admissible quadrant N>=0, P>=0, which is the only region where a pool content is defined. Substituting max(pool,0) inside these ratios only is the identity for N>=0, P>=0, so no admissible trajectory changes; it removes the pole on the ray N=-R*P that a Runge-Kutta trial stage can reach when a pool is driven to zero.",recomputed,"Bit-identity claim TESTED 2026-08-15 and UPHELD: applied alone to HEAD (sandbox sc_pole), model_report --days 30 --lsb-grid --nitrogen returns a CSV numerically identical to the anchor in all 108 data rows (sha256 equal after neutralising the label column). Axis is neutral for every measure in the yardstick; it is an integrability guard, not a change to the physics."
nutrients.Michaelis_Menten_constant_nitrogen,0.125,umolN cm-3,T3,Tedone2020,"§2.2.7 (Eq 2.2.22), ""k_n = 0.125 umolN/cm3""",,read_paper,"ADDED THIS SESSION -- was absent from the ledger. Value verified verbatim at the locator. This row also fixes the unit of the two soil-content rows: since kn is umolN cm-3, ns must be too, i.e. 1 unit == 1 mM. LIVE (0.95% change)."
nutrients.Michaelis_Menten_constant_phosphorus,0.006736,umolP cm-3,T3,Tedone2020,"§2.2.7 (Eq 2.2.22), ""k_p = 0.006736 umolP/cm3""",,read_paper,ADDED THIS SESSION -- was absent from the ledger. Value verified verbatim at the locator.
gas_exchange.ambient_CO2_concentration,400.0,umol mol-1,T4,,,"Ambient atmospheric CO2 at the time the reference experiments were run (~400 ppm, 2014-2016). A property of the growth atmosphere, not of the plant; bounded by the atmospheric record.",unit_check,"ADDED THIS SESSION -- was absent from the ledger. Note the reference plants were grown in ambient-air chambers, so 400 is appropriate, but the exact figure is a round number, not a logged chamber measurement."
gas_exchange.CO2_compensation_point,42.0,umol mol-1,T6,,,,,"ADDED THIS SESSION -- was absent from the ledger, and REMAINS UNSOURCED. Gamma* = 42 umol mol-1 at 25 C is a widely used Farquhar-model value, but no primary source could be located for it in this project: the bibliography has no entry that states it, and the value is not in the Tedone text. Reported as unsourced rather than attributed to a plausible-looking citation. It is a work-list item, not a paper claim."
gas_exchange.michaelis_constant_CO2,404.9,umol mol-1,T6,,,,,"ADDED THIS SESSION -- was absent from the ledger, and REMAINS UNSOURCED. Kc = 404.9 is the value normally attributed to Bernacchi et al. 2001, but that paper is a TOBACCO study whose full text is not open access here, so the value could not be located at any stated locator in the source. Attributing it would be citing a number through its reputation rather than its source. T6 pending access to the primary text."
gas_exchange.michaelis_constant_O2,278.4,mmol mol-1,T6,,,,,"ADDED THIS SESSION -- was absent from the ledger, and REMAINS UNSOURCED. Ko = 278.4, same situation as Kc above."
hardcoded.growth.lambda_sb_nitrogen_divisor,12.0,umolN cm-3,T6,,,,,"NOT IN ANY CONFIG FILE. Hardcoded at src/model/growth.c:119 (n = nitrogen_soil/12.0) and reused in R_plus() at growth.c:131. It sets the soil-N level at which the growth gate min(n,p)>=1 opens, so it is a threshold parameter with no source, no unit statement, and no ledger row until now. Measured: with the shipped soil N of 15.0 the gate is open and lambda_sb passes through unreduced; at 11.9 it closes. UNSOURCED."
hardcoded.growth.lambda_sb_phosphorus_divisor,0.15,umolP cm-3,T6,,,,,"NOT IN ANY CONFIG FILE. Hardcoded at src/model/growth.c:119 (p = phosphorus_soil/0.15). Numerically identical to the shipped phosphorus_soil_content, so p == 1.0 exactly and the gate sits on its threshold by construction. UNSOURCED, and the coincidence should be removed rather than documented."
hardcoded.photosynthesis.base_scale,1.10,dimensionless (umol hexose gFW-1 h-1 per umol CO2 m-2 s-1),T4,Sulpice2014; AtkinsonAtkin2024; C3_quantum_yield_ceiling,"mmc3 sheet ""Growth components"" rows 2-3 (headers), row 5 ""Assimilation rate (umol C / g FW h)"", row 10 ""Assimilation (umol glc equiv / g FW h)"", row 24 ""% assimilation rate to starch synth""; mmc3 sheet ""Growth in day and night"" row 2 headers + row 10 definition ""A = photosynthesis (measured at end of day)"" and row 14 ""Net C assimilation per 24 h cycle = total A over the light period - total R over the night""; mmc2 sheet ""clean dataset-all data"" column ""average DW content""; N_data.csv column ""LMA  (mean value, n=3)"" (34 leaf rows)","kappa converts an AREA-based net assimilation rate to a MASS-based hexose rate. The dimensional identity is kappa = SLA_FW [m2 gFW-1] * 3600 [s h-1] / 6 [mol CO2 per mol hexose] = 600 * SLA_DW / (FW:DW). THREE INDEPENDENT ROUTES, each written out. ROUTE 1 (Sulpice per-gFW ratio): mmc3 row 10 gives 16.61193/16.75550/18.23333/15.39860 umol glc equiv gFW-1 h-1 at 4/6/8/12 h. Sheet ""Growth in day and night"" defines A as photosynthesis measured at end of day and computes net 24 h assimilation SEPARATELY as AD - RD, so row 10 is a LIGHT-PERIOD GROSS rate per gram FRESH weight, not net of night respiration; it is net of daytime leaf Rd only, which is what the model FvCB branch also returns. Dividing by the model An_area under the SAME light gives kappa = 3.301 (square PAR 160, An=5.0735), 4.262 (half-sine peak 160, An=3.9303) or 1.886 (production half-sine peak 1200, An=8.8813). The route is therefore SCHEDULE-DEPENDENT and does not bound kappa by itself. ROUTE 2 (C3 quantum-yield ceiling): apparent QY cannot exceed ~0.06-0.08 mol CO2 per mol photon. At PAR 160 the shipped SLA 0.025 implies An = 13.404 -> QY 0.0838, ABOVE the ceiling; SLA 0.06135 implies An = 5.462 -> QY 0.0341, admissible. This route is ONE-SIDED: it rules out the shipped SLA but fixes no value. ROUTE 3 (measured LMA): N_data.csv 34 leaf rows give mean LMA 19.0206 gDW m-2, so SLA = 1/mean(LMA) = 0.05257 or mean(1/LMA) = 0.06135 m2 gDW-1, per-row range 0.02834-0.13986; the shipped 0.025 is below the measured MINIMUM. By the code form kappa = 44*SLA_DW this is 2.313-2.699; by the dimensional form 50*SLA_DW it is 2.629-3.068. INTERNAL CONSISTENCY (both checks pass): Aarea/Amass reproduces LMA to -3.88% and Rarea/Rmass to -3.54% on the same rows, so the units are being read correctly. SEPARATE FINDING: at the reference SLA the dimensional value is 600*0.025/12 = 1.2500, whereas the code computes 1.10*SLA/0.025 = 44*SLA_DW. The code coefficient is 44 where dimensional analysis requires 50, i.e. the shipped constant is 12.0% BELOW its own dimensional value at the FW:DW ratio of 12 that mmc2 reports.",recomputed; measured (an_probe at fixed PAR); dimensional analysis,"TIER RAISED T5->T4: bounded by conservation and by the C3 quantum-yield ceiling, not fitted. NOT IN ANY CONFIG FILE - hardcoded as base_scale at src/model/photosynthesis.c:233, with ref_specific_leaf_area 0.025 at :234, so the config field gas_exchange.convert_to_photosynthesis_per_gram_per_hour (24000.0) is inert and SLA is the only lever. THE THREE ROUTES DO NOT AGREE ON A VALUE and must not be averaged: route 1 spans 1.886-4.262 depending purely on which light schedule is put in the denominator, and the ""2.95x / mean 2.67x"" figures previously quoted implicitly assumed a SQUARE 160 chamber that does not exist at this commit - update_light_conditions() (photosynthesis.c:341) imposes a half-sine at every setting, and --chamber only lowers its peak to 160 (mean 101.9). What the three routes DO agree on is one-sided: kappa 1.10 is TOO SMALL, and the shipped SLA 0.025 is below the measured minimum. The dimensionally correct value at the shipped SLA is 1.2500. COST OF APPLYING IT (measured, clean sandbox, stall-aware): integrability is NOT bounded by kappa but by absorbed daily carbon. Under the production half-sine (peak 1200) 24/24 fails at 12 h from kappa 1.30 and at 8 h from kappa 2.00; under the chamber half-sine (peak 160) all four photoperiods hold 24/24 up to kappa 3.245 and fail only at 4.0. The collapse boundary sits at 92-157 umol hexose gFW-1 d-1 of absorbed carbon in BOTH schedules. This CONTRADICTS the earlier claim that kappa 3.25 collapses integrability to 3/28 at 12 h even under matched chamber light: at matched light it is 24/24. RAISING KAPPA ALONE IS NOT ADMISSIBLE: it needs a sink that does not exist - see docs/revision/conversion_settled.md."
hardcoded.photosynthesis.ref_specific_leaf_area,0.025,m2 gFW-1,T2,,,"Hardcoded reference SLA in convert_to_photosynthesis_per_gram_per_hour(): the function returns net_photosynthesis_rate * 1.10 * (SLA/0.025), so this constant only sets what SLA value counts as unity. It is a normalisation, not an independent parameter -- but it means the config specific_leaf_area acts purely as a ratio against it.",recomputed,NOT IN ANY CONFIG FILE. Hardcoded at src/model/photosynthesis.c.
hardcoded.photosynthesis.quantum_yield_phi,0.385,mol e- mol-1 photons,T6,,,,,"NOT IN ANY CONFIG FILE. Hardcoded in compute_J() (src/model/photosynthesis.c:126). The code comment attributes the non-rectangular hyperbola form to Farquhar et al. 1980 and the curvature to Farquhar & Wong 1984, but NEITHER key is in paper/v2/master_ref.bib, so the attribution cannot be checked and no locator exists. UNSOURCED as shipped."
hardcoded.photosynthesis.curvature_theta,0.7,-,T6,,,,,NOT IN ANY CONFIG FILE. Hardcoded in compute_J() (src/model/photosynthesis.c:127). Same missing-citation problem as phi.
hardcoded.jarvis.b1,0.6,-,T6,,,,,"NOT IN ANY CONFIG FILE. Hardcoded at src/model/photosynthesis.c:473 in the Jarvis conductance model. paper/v1/cas-sc-template.tex lists the whole Jarvis block with a dagger, i.e. flagged, and no source. UNSOURCED."
hardcoded.jarvis.b2,0.002,-,T6,,,,,NOT IN ANY CONFIG FILE. Hardcoded at src/model/photosynthesis.c:474. UNSOURCED.
hardcoded.photosynthesis.ci_init_fraction,0.7,-,T4,,,"Initial guess Ci = 0.7*Ca for the intercellular-CO2 iteration (src/model/photosynthesis.c:413). A starting value for a converging solve, not a parameter: it is bounded by 0 < Ci < Ca and the iterate_ci_tol loop overwrites it. Affects iteration count, not the solution.",recomputed,"NOT IN ANY CONFIG FILE. Numerical initial guess; listed for completeness, not a model parameter."
DEFECT.algebraic.uptake_cost_evaluation_order,,,T4,conservation,src/model/algebraic.c:86 (call) vs :127/:131 (assignments),"uptake_cost() is called at algebraic.c:86 with s.nutrients.nitrogen_uptake and s.nutrients.phosphorus_uptake as arguments, but those two fields are only assigned 41 and 45 lines LATER, at :127 and :131. The call therefore reads their incoming values, which are 0.0 on every evaluation, so uptake_cost is identically zero everywhere including inside the ODE right-hand side. MEASURED: moving the single call below both assignments (the whole change, one file, verified by diff against the baseline export) makes nutrient uptake a sink worth 14.8-24.1% of gross assimilation at kappa 1.10. It is not a tool artefact: the probe used here recomputes every flux from the live solver state, which does carry X_N and X_P, and still measured exactly zero at HEAD.",measured (isolated single-change sandbox); conservation,"CORRECTS A PRIOR DIAGNOSIS: the zero share_uptake was attributed to SimulationResult not carrying N/P, i.e. to tool blindness. That is true of the model_report reconstruction but is NOT the cause. The cause is evaluation order in the model itself, and it suppresses a real sink of 15-24% of assimilation. Under the fix, closure still holds (residual <=0.35%) and respiration falls from 29.9-34.2% to 24.2-27.5% of assimilation, i.e. toward the measured 10-18% but still above it."
DEFECT.growth.no_carbon_price_on_biomass,,,T4,conservation,src/model/carbohydrates.c:106 (sucrose_production) vs src/model/growth.c:12 (leaf_growth),"Integrating the two carbohydrate ODEs over a closed diel cycle gives, exactly, int A dt = int [uptake_cost + transport_cost + r_m*S + lambda_L*nes] dt: the four sucrose sinks alone account for ALL gross assimilation and starch is an intra-day buffer with zero net cycle flux. Biomass growth is NOT among the four. leaf_growth() is lambda_sb*(1-alpha)*lambda_L*nes*B_leaf, i.e. it is DRIVEN BY the same phloem-load flux that debits sucrose but carries an extra factor of biomass and is never charged against it. Consequently biomass has no carbon price and the conversion of exported sucrose into new mass is set by the fitted lambda_sb (0.003843-0.005850), not by a stoichiometry.",conservation; measured (budget_probe closure 0.02-0.35% at every kappa and photoperiod),"This is why raising kappa cannot be absorbed: the extra carbon has nowhere to go that is priced. Sulpice mmc3 row 17 measures protein synthesis alone at 21.2-29.8% of daily carbon gain, a real growth sink the structure lacks. Adding it requires a C-per-gram stoichiometry, which is a structural change, not a parameter change."
hardcoded.photosynthesis.leaf_biomass_discarded,(void),-,T6,,src/model/photosynthesis.c:230-242,"convert_to_photosynthesis_per_gram_per_hour() accepts leaf_biomass and discards it with (void)leaf_biomass. Dimensionally this is CORRECT as a per-gram rate: total assimilation is An*SLA*B_l and dividing by B_l to get the per-gram rate cancels the mass, so PH = An*SLA*3600/6 is complete. Reinstating B_l as a multiplicative factor would introduce an error.",source read; rosette-size comparison against the atlas,"FOURTH accepted-and-discarded parameter found this session (after max_sucrose in night_efficiency_starch, lambda_c via the disconnected feedback, and the max_starch config key). What the argument was for is SIZE DEPENDENCE, which the model lacks: at day 30 the 12 h plant has 160.08 gFW of leaf = 0.8805 m2 at the atlas SLA, against a real 3-week Col-0 rosette of 0.0105 m2 (atlas, 29 leaves, 10500 mm2) -- 83.9x -- and every square metre sees full PAR with no shading. A self-shading / light-interception term is the missing physics. Likely explanation for the monotone residual pattern +17.2/+0.4/-15.4/-24.1% left after the best single lambda_sb. STRUCTURAL CHANGE: needs its own source and its own measurement."
carbohydrates.k_vacuole_in,0.1,h-1,T5,Seydel2025,ratio from Suppl. Table S5; the rate itself unsourced,"Sets the exchange TIMESCALE tau = 1/(k_in+k_out) = 7.04 h; the equilibrium partition is fixed separately by k_in/k_out. MEASURED sensitivity at the fixed sourced ratio 2.3834, k_in in {0.02, 0.05, 0.10, 0.30, 1.00} h-1 (tau 35.2 to 0.70 h): daily-mean MAPE varies by only 0.79 pts (58.67-59.46%), confirming the level is set by the ratio alone; but cycle CV varies materially (mean CV error 8.97, 8.77, 8.37, 5.13, 7.13 pts), so k_in does control the amplitude. Retained at 0.10 h-1 rather than tuned to the CV-optimal 0.30 h-1.","simulation, .sandboxes/v2","The ONLY free rate in the vacuole pair, and it has a real effect on amplitude -- not a nuisance parameter. Not tuned: moving it to the CV-optimal 0.30 h-1 would gain ~3 pts of CV agreement at the cost of turning a retained value into a fitted one. A measured tonoplast transporter V_max would fix it; not found (paywalled), and at S ~ K_m = 21 mM (Kaiser & Heber 1984) a first-order linearisation would be invalid anyway."
carbohydrates.k_vacuole_out,0.041959,h-1,T2,Seydel2025,"Plant Physiol 198:kiaf117, Suppl. Table S5 sheet ST3, control rows, n=5","Set so that k_vacuole_in/k_vacuole_out equals the MEASURED vacuole/cytosol sucrose amount ratio 21.57/9.05 = 2.3834. At equilibrium the exchange terms cancel in ds_cyt/dt, so s_vac/s_cyt = k_in/k_out exactly and the ratio is an observable, not a fitted constant: k_out = 0.10/2.3834 = 0.041959. Verified in simulation: realised ratio 2.3835-2.4057 across photoperiods, cytosolic mean unchanged to <=0.30%.","simulation, .sandboxes/v2, 4/4 integrating","Replaces 0.08 (ratio 1.25), which was T6 and justified by 'Lohaus et al. (2007) Planta 227:143-156' -- a locator that does not resolve (checked against CrossRef); it is a corrupted variant of Nadwodnik & Lohaus 2008 Planta 227:1079-1089, which measures Plantago/Prunus/Apium, not Arabidopsis. The same source's '70-95% tonoplast-sequestered' claim is also unsupported: measured Arabidopsis is 53.6% by amount, and by CONCENTRATION the vacuole is the most dilute compartment (2.4 mM vs 23.6 mM cytosolic), because it is 23.5x the cytosolic volume."
growth.lambda_sb,0.00614038,gFW per umol C6,T5,heldout_lsb,tools/heldout_lsb.c; docs/revision/sucrose_conclusion.md,"ONE shared value replacing the per-photoperiod table {0.003843, 0.004433, 0.005246, 0.005850}. Fitted across all four photoperiods jointly, i.e. one parameter instead of four. Held-out test over seven train/test splits gives a shared value in 0.00583-0.00645 with in-sample 4.75% and held-out 0.18-12.35%. Chamber light: RGR MAPE 4.686% (per-photoperiod table 20.736%) at 4/4 integrating.",".sandboxes/v2 arm B, model_report --lambda-sb","Still fitted, and labelled so. The point is that it is ONE fitted number rather than four, and that it PREDICTS unseen photoperiods, which the per-photoperiod table cannot do by construction. Requires model_report's hard-coded LAMBDA_SB[] table to be bypassed (--lambda-sb flag added in .sandboxes/v2); without that flag a config edit is silently overwritten at setup(). Supersedes the per-photoperiod table previously recorded here (0.00587 as the single config default, with {0.003843, 0.004433, 0.005246, 0.005850} hard-coded in the tools)."
